Subject: [PATCH] Port native RemoteServer workers and sockets to Windows
Base: DoltLite v0.50.12 with local patches 0001-0009 applied

This patch enables the native RemoteServer on Windows and preserves the
existing public SQL and HTTP interfaces. Keep these behaviors when refreshing
the staged upstream sources:
- Use SRW locks, condition variables, and CRT threads on Windows; use POSIX
  mutexes, conditions, and pthreads on macOS/Linux.
- Preserve full-width Windows SOCKET handles through listen, accept, polling,
  active-worker tracking, shutdown, timeout configuration, and close.
- Initialize Winsock and Mbed TLS threading exactly once before concurrent
  network or TLS use.
- Keep the TLS client and server connections as distinct opaque C types. The
  server must not pass its connection object into embedded client functions.
- Send TLS close-notify while a worker socket is tracked, then untrack before
  final connection cleanup so shutdown cannot race with a reused handle.
- Apply one Mbed TLS feature configuration to the amalgamation, added TLS
  server/threading units, and TLS sidecar. The amalgamation intentionally omits
  those server-only implementations, so compile them as staged units rather
  than relying on declarations or stubs.
- Use alternate mutex hooks for TLS 1.3/PSA global state and the shared server
  DRBG; do not rely on separate per-connection contexts for thread safety.
- Keep Windows worker sockets nonblocking and check server stop between
  bounded readiness waits; preserve per-I/O timeouts and worker-owned final close.

